  <h2>What is APatch?</h2>
  <p>
    APatch is an open-source rooting solution created by bmax121. Like
    <a href="/kernelsu">KernelSU</a>, it works at the kernel level — but
    instead of replacing or building around the kernel, it patches the existing
    kernel image itself. The manager app checks your kernel's compatibility
    when you patch.
  </p>

  <h2>What it gives you</h2>
  <p>
    Superuser (root) access with per-app prompts, plus two kinds of modules:
    KPModules (KPM), which run code inside the kernel, and AndroidPatch Modules
    (APM), which change system behavior without editing
    <code>/system</code> in the style of <a href="/magisk">Magisk</a> modules.
  </p>

  <h2>Before you root</h2>
  <p>
    APatch requires an unlocked bootloader, and rooting trips integrity checks
    that some apps — banking and payment apps above all — actively look for.
    Download APatch <em>only</em> from the official GitHub page; files from
    unknown sources can be malicious. Knowing your exact device and bootloader
    state is step one — our free
    <a href="/scan">browser-based scan</a> reports both over USB.
  </p>
